  "evidences": [
    {
      "id": "ev_9",
      "evidence_type": "report_text",
      "report_id": "Kaspersky_Evolution-of-Cyber-Threats-in-the-Corporate-Sector(Dec-10-2015)",
      "locator": {
        "page": 4,
        "section": "body",
        "sentence_id": "p4_s2"
      },
      "text": "The Carbanak campaign became a vivid example of how APT-class targeted attacks have shifted focus to financial organizations.",
      "language": "en",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "note": "narrative sentence evidence",
      "source": "document"
    },
    {
      "id": "ev_11",
      "evidence_type": "report_text",
      "report_id": "Kaspersky_Evolution-of-Cyber-Threats-in-the-Corporate-Sector(Dec-10-2015)",
      "locator": {
        "page": 4,
        "section": "body",
        "sentence_id": "p4_s4"
      },
      "text": "However, the Carbanak campaign has also targeted victims in the US, Germany and China.",
      "language": "en",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "note": "narrative sentence evidence",
      "source": "document"
    },
    {
      "id": "ev_12",
      "evidence_type": "report_text",
      "report_id": "Kaspersky_Evolution-of-Cyber-Threats-in-the-Corporate-Sector(Dec-10-2015)",
      "locator": {
        "page": 5,
        "section": "body",
        "sentence_id": "p5_s1"
      },
      "text": "One example of a targeted attack that may have been hunting for such information is Wild Neutron (aka Jripbot and Morpho).",
      "language": "en",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "note": "narrative sentence evidence",
      "source": "document"
    },
    {
      "id": "ev_15",
      "evidence_type": "report_text",
      "report_id": "Kaspersky_Evolution-of-Cyber-Threats-in-the-Corporate-Sector(Dec-10-2015)",
      "locator": {
        "page": 5,
        "section": "body",
        "sentence_id": "p5_s4"
      },
      "text": "However, about a year later Kaspersky Lab observed that Wild Neutron had resumed operations.",
      "language": "en",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "note": "narrative sentence evidence",
      "source": "document"
    },
    {
      "id": "ev_18",
      "evidence_type": "report_text",
      "report_id": "Kaspersky_Evolution-of-Cyber-Threats-in-the-Corporate-Sector(Dec-10-2015)",
      "locator": {
        "page": 5,
        "section": "body",
        "sentence_id": "p5_s7"
      },
      "text": "Stolen Acer certificate in the Wild Neutron installer The trend towards the diversification of APT attacks is well illustrated by the change in targets attacked by the Chinese cybercriminal group Winnti .",
      "language": "en",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "note": "narrative sentence evidence",
      "source": "document"
    },
    {
      "id": "ev_21",
      "evidence_type": "report_text",
      "report_id": "Kaspersky_Evolution-of-Cyber-Threats-in-the-Corporate-Sector(Dec-10-2015)",
      "locator": {
        "page": 6,
        "section": "body",
        "sentence_id": "p6_s2"
      },
      "text": "The group, dubbed the Desert Falcons , is the first Arab actor to conduct full-blown cyberespionage attacks.",
      "language": "en",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "note": "narrative sentence evidence",
      "source": "document"
    },
    {
      "id": "ev_23",
      "evidence_type": "report_text",
      "report_id": "Kaspersky_Evolution-of-Cyber-Threats-in-the-Corporate-Sector(Dec-10-2015)",
      "locator": {
        "page": 6,
        "section": "body",
        "sentence_id": "p6_s4"
      },
      "text": "Another group named Blue Termite attacked organizations and companies in Japan:",
      "language": "en",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "note": "narrative sentence evidence",
      "source": "document"
    },
    {
      "id": "ev_29",
      "evidence_type": "report_text",
      "report_id": "Kaspersky_Evolution-of-Cyber-Threats-in-the-Corporate-Sector(Dec-10-2015)",
      "locator": {
        "page": 8,
        "section": "body",
        "sentence_id": "p8_s3"
      },
      "text": "In 2015, one or more malware attack was blocked on 58% of corporate user computers, which is a 3 p.p.",
      "language": "en",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "note": "narrative sentence evidence",
      "source": "document"
    },
    {
      "id": "ev_36",
      "evidence_type": "report_text",
      "report_id": "Kaspersky_Evolution-of-Cyber-Threats-in-the-Corporate-Sector(Dec-10-2015)",
      "locator": {
        "page": 11,
        "section": "body",
        "sentence_id": "p11_s2"
      },
      "text": "• exploits for vulnerabilities found in office applications are used three times more often than in attacks on home users; • use of malicious files signed with valid digital certificates; • use of legitimate programs in attacks, allowing the attackers to go undetected for longer.",
      "language": "en",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "note": "narrative sentence evidence",
      "source": "document"
    },
    {
      "id": "ev_50",
      "evidence_type": "report_text",
      "report_id": "Kaspersky_Evolution-of-Cyber-Threats-in-the-Corporate-Sector(Dec-10-2015)",
      "locator": {
        "page": 14,
        "section": "body",
        "sentence_id": "p14_s2"
      },
      "text": "Ransomware Encryption Trojans were long considered to be a threat to home users only.",
      "language": "en",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "note": "narrative sentence evidence",
      "source": "document"
    },
    {
      "id": "ev_51",
      "evidence_type": "report_text",
      "report_id": "Kaspersky_Evolution-of-Cyber-Threats-in-the-Corporate-Sector(Dec-10-2015)",
      "locator": {
        "page": 14,
        "section": "body",
        "sentence_id": "p14_s3"
      },
      "text": "Nowadays, however, we see ransomware actors paying more attention to organizations as targets.",
      "language": "en",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "note": "narrative sentence evidence",
      "source": "document"
    },
    {
      "id": "ev_52",
      "evidence_type": "report_text",
      "report_id": "Kaspersky_Evolution-of-Cyber-Threats-in-the-Corporate-Sector(Dec-10-2015)",
      "locator": {
        "page": 14,
        "section": "body",
        "sentence_id": "p14_s4"
      },
      "text": "In 2015, Kaspersky Lab solutions detected ransomware on more than 50,000 computers in corporate networks, which is double the figure for 2014 .",
      "language": "en",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "note": "narrative sentence evidence",
      "source": "document"
    },
    {
      "id": "ev_58",
      "evidence_type": "report_text",
      "report_id": "Kaspersky_Evolution-of-Cyber-Threats-in-the-Corporate-Sector(Dec-10-2015)",
      "locator": {
        "page": 15,
        "section": "body",
        "sentence_id": "p15_s4"
      },
      "text": "TOP 10 encryptor Trojan families Family % attacked users* 1 Scatter 21 2 Onion 16 3 Cryakl 15 4 Snocry 11 5 Cryptodef 8 6 Rakhni 7 7 Crypmod 6 8 Shade 5 9 Mor 3 10 Crypren 2",
      "language": "en",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "note": "narrative sentence evidence",
      "source": "document"
    },
    {
      "id": "ev_60",
      "evidence_type": "report_text",
      "report_id": "Kaspersky_Evolution-of-Cyber-Threats-in-the-Corporate-Sector(Dec-10-2015)",
      "locator": {
        "page": 15,
        "section": "body",
        "sentence_id": "p15_s6"
      },
      "text": "The Scatter family of Trojans occupies first place.",
      "language": "en",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "note": "narrative sentence evidence",
      "source": "document"
    },
    {
      "id": "ev_62",
      "evidence_type": "report_text",
      "report_id": "Kaspersky_Evolution-of-Cyber-Threats-in-the-Corporate-Sector(Dec-10-2015)",
      "locator": {
        "page": 15,
        "section": "body",
        "sentence_id": "p15_s8"
      },
      "text": "Scatter Trojans are multi-module, multi-purpose script-based malicious programs.",
      "language": "en",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "note": "narrative sentence evidence",
      "source": "document"
    },
    {
      "id": "ev_66",
      "evidence_type": "report_text",
      "report_id": "Kaspersky_Evolution-of-Cyber-Threats-in-the-Corporate-Sector(Dec-10-2015)",
      "locator": {
        "page": 16,
        "section": "body",
        "sentence_id": "p16_s2"
      },
      "text": "Attacks like this can lead to huge losses, comparable to those caused by the Wiper malware attacks that destroyed data in corporate networks.",
      "language": "en",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "note": "narrative sentence evidence",
      "source": "document"
    },
    {
      "id": "ev_71",
